config ACTUATOR_ICL57
	bool "iCL-RS integrated closed-loop stepper actuator (Modbus RTU)"
	depends on ACTUATOR
	depends on DT_HAS_ROSTERLOH_ACTUATOR_ICL57_ENABLED
	select MODBUS
	select UART_INTERRUPT_DRIVEN
	default y
	help
	  StepperOnline/Leadshine iCL-RS series integrated closed-loop stepper
	  motors over RS485 Modbus RTU. Each instance is a child of a
	  zephyr,modbus-serial bus node; the driver binds to the parent Modbus
	  interface by name and streams absolute position setpoints via the PR0
	  immediate-trigger block.

config ACTUATOR_ICL57_MAPPED_POLL
	bool "Poll feedback through the drive's register-mapping block"
	depends on ACTUATOR_ICL57
	default y
	help
	  Program the iCL-RS register-mapping area (manual section 4.5) at every
	  enable so one FC03 returns motion state, feedback position, feedback
	  velocity and the digital inputs, instead of three transactions per
	  poll plus one DI read per setpoint. Roughly a 4x cut in bus traffic on
	  a three-motor bus, which is the documented cause of mispaired reads.

	  On iCL57-RS13 drives the values read back at 0x0F00 (the manual's
	  worked example; its prose says 0x0F10, which reads back the TARGET
	  addresses). The driver probes both addresses and
	  trusts the block only once its mapped Pr0.00 word reads back as
	  counts-per-rev; if neither passes it logs a warning and keeps the
	  direct reads, so enabling this cannot silently change what feeds the
	  setpoint path.

	  On by default: homing and position-mode moves across ~50 low-word wraps
	  of the mapped 32-bit position showed no tearing, and bus load on a
	  three-drive bus fell from ~75 to 28-32 transactions a second.

config ACTUATOR_ICL57_BUS_STATS
	bool "Log a per-second summary of Modbus traffic"
	depends on ACTUATOR_ICL57
	help
	  One INF line a second: transactions, failures, how many took over
	  30 ms, the slowest, and the longest gap between two setpoint writes to
	  any drive, plus one line per failed or slow transaction: the way to
	  tell a motion stall from a bus timeout. Separate from debug logging on
	  purpose: debug logging floods the log, which drops lines under load,
	  and a summary covers its whole second even when other lines are lost.
